description:
What: Implement a production IpfsBlockStore backed by rust-ipfs 0.15.0.
Algorithm:
1. In crates/reader/src/post/ipfs_write.rs, add:
   pub struct RustIpfsStore { ipfs: rust_ipfs::Ipfs }
   impl RustIpfsStore {
       pub async fn new() -> Result<Self, String> {
           let ipfs = rust_ipfs::builder::DefaultIpfsBuilder::new()
               .start().await
               .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
           Ok(Self { ipfs })
       }
   }
2. Implement IpfsBlockStore for RustIpfsStore:
   put_raw_block: compute sha2-256, build CID(v1, RAW=0x55, hash), call ipfs.put_block(&block).await, return cid
   get_raw_block: call ipfs.get_block(cid).await, return block.data().to_vec()
3. Map rust_ipfs::Error to IpfsWriteError:
   - "not found" messages -> IpfsWriteError::NotFound
   - other errors -> IpfsWriteError::WriteFailed
4. Add test: put_raw_block then get_raw_block roundtrip returns same bytes
Defensive: never unwrap(); always map_err(); Block::new can fail (verify CID matches data).
Acceptance: test_rust_ipfs_roundtrip passes; cargo test clean.
